    "title": "fix: detect glob-star-in-branch and repetition overlap as ReDoS-risky extglobs (CVE-2026-112366)",
    "body": "## Problem\n\nCVE-2026-112366 / SNYK-JS-PICOMATCH-21248802 (CVSS 8.7 High): Patterns\nlike `+(*)`, `+(*a)`, `+(a*)`, and `*(a*|b)` trigger exponential regex\nbacktracking, blocking the Node.js event loop with inputs as short as\n25-30 characters.\n\nThis also addresses the multi-character prefix overlap bypass reported\nin #175 \u2014 patterns like `+(ab|abab)` that escaped the existing\n`hasRepeatedCharPrefixOverlap` safeguard.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`analyzeRepeatedExtglob` had two blind spots:\n\n1. **Glob stars in branches** \u2014 A glob `*` inside a `+()` or `*()`\n   branch compiles to `[^/]*?`, creating a nested quantifier\n   (`(?:[^/]*?X)+`) with exponential partition ambiguity. The existing\n   checks only caught wildcard-only branches in multi-branch patterns.\n\n2. **Multi-char repetition overlap** \u2014 The existing\n   `hasRepeatedCharPrefixOverlap` only detected single-character\n   repeats (e.g., `a|aa`). Multi-character cases like `ab|abab` \u2014 where\n   one branch is a whole-string repetition of another \u2014 were missed.\n\n## Fix\n\n- **`branchContainsGlobStar`**: detects unescaped `*` outside bracket\n  classes, distinguishing glob stars (`*x`) from extglob quantifiers\n  (`*(x)`) via `branch[i+1] !== '('`.\n- **`hasBranchRepetitionOverlap`**: replaces the single-char-only check\n  with a general \"is one branch a repetition of another\" test.\n- Both checks run early in `analyzeRepeatedExtglob`, before the existing\n  star-sequence and recursion analysis. The `maxExtglobRecursion: false`\n  escape hatch continues to disable all safeguards.\n\nCommon patterns like `+(js|jsx)`, `+(foo|bar)`, `*(foo|bar)`, and\n`*.+(js|jsx)` are **not affected** \u2014 the fix correctly identifies that\n`jsx` is not a repetition of `js`.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBefore fix (`+(*a)` against `'a'.repeat(30)+'!'`): **8,744 ms**\nAfter fix: **<0.1 ms**\n\nBefore fix (`+(ab|abab)` against `'ab'.repeat(40)+'c'`): **1,779 ms**\nAfter fix: **<0.1 ms**\n\nFull test suite: 1986 passing, 0 failing.\n\n## Test changes\n\n- 4 existing assertions updated: they previously asserted that\n  vulnerable patterns like `+(*)c` and `*(a*|b)` would match\n  functionally. They now assert literalized behavior.\n- 3 new test blocks: CVE-specific regression tests, repetition-overlap\n  tests (including positive tests for safe patterns), and\n  extglob-quantifier-vs-glob-star distinction tests.\n\n## Credit\n\nVulnerability reported by maximilliangrand and Zachariah Mithani (Snyk\nadvisory). Multi-char overlap bypass reported by Raunak Gupta (#175).\n\nFixes #175",
